WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:20.485
"Really? You have a mystery for us to solve?" Maggie asked Nathan eagerly.

2
00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:26.613
Henry stared at the five-dollar bill that Nathan had just slapped down on the lemonade stand.

3
00:00:26.614 --> 00:00:29.533
He felt a flutter of excitement.

4
00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:31.990
"Cool!" he said.

5
00:00:31.991 --> 00:00:36.059
"What's the mystery?" Cole sounded excited too.

6
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.632
"It's about my little sister Nora," Nathan told them.

7
00:00:39.633 --> 00:00:42.642
"She's been acting weird lately."

8
00:00:42.643 --> 00:00:48.374
Henry's excited feeling faded. He traded a look with Maggie and Cole.

9
00:00:48.375 --> 00:00:52.952
Cole looked disappointed. Maggie rolled her eyes.

10
00:00:52.953 --> 00:00:56.969
"What's the mystery about that?" Maggie asked Nathan.

11
00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:01.439
"No offense, but Nora always acts kind of weird."

12
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:10.713
"Yeah." Cole laughed. "Remember when she wore those pink pants every day for a week, and wanted everyone to call her Princess Pretty Pants?"

13
00:01:10.714 --> 00:01:13.608
"That's nothing," Maggie said.

14
00:01:13.609 --> 00:01:18.115
"What about the time she pretended she was an alien from outer space?"

15
00:01:18.116 --> 00:01:26.726
Henry nodded. Nora was only five years old, but she was famous in the neighborhood for doing strange stuff.

16
00:01:26.727 --> 00:01:31.678
"She argues with everybody about everything," Henry added.

17
00:01:31.679 --> 00:01:36.743
"And she's always dragging her stuffed animals around and pretending they're real."

18
00:01:36.744 --> 00:01:39.028
Nathan grinned.

19
00:01:39.029 --> 00:01:43.861
"She pretends her stuffed animals are real because she wants a pet so badly.

20
00:01:43.862 --> 00:01:50.030
She begged for a puppy for her fourth birthday, but Mom and Dad said no pets."

21
00:01:50.031 --> 00:01:54.433
"So it's no mystery that she's acting weird," Cole told Nathan again.

22
00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:59.312
Nathan shook his head. "This is different," he said.

23
00:01:59.313 --> 00:02:05.101
"Mom and Dad are really worried. They think Nora has been sleepwalking!

24
00:02:05.102 --> 00:02:10.281
They've caught her a couple of times walking around outside after dark."

25
00:02:10.282 --> 00:02:13.911
"Nora's been sleepwalking?" Henry said.

26
00:02:13.912 --> 00:02:18.748
"That sounds kind of serious, but it's not really a mystery."

27
00:02:18.749 --> 00:02:22.965
"I said they think she's been sleepwalking," Nathan said.

28
00:02:22.966 --> 00:02:24.986
"I think she's faking!"

29
00:02:24.987 --> 00:02:28.047
"Why do you think that?" Henry asked.

30
00:02:28.048 --> 00:02:30.695
"It's just a feeling," Nathan said.

31
00:02:30.696 --> 00:02:35.858
"I think she's up to something sneaky, but I'm not sure what it is."

32
00:02:35.859 --> 00:02:43.001
Maggie shrugged. "So what? Why do you care if she's pretending to sleepwalk?"

33
00:02:43.002 --> 00:02:46.450
"I just want to find out the truth," Nathan said.

34
00:02:46.451 --> 00:02:50.573
"Like I said, my parents are really worried about her.

35
00:02:50.574 --> 00:02:53.980
They're planning to take her to the doctor next week.

36
00:02:53.981 --> 00:02:57.561
If she's really sleepwalking, that's okay.

37
00:02:57.562 --> 00:03:04.090
But if she's faking it, she's making them worry for nothing! That's not fair."

38
00:03:04.091 --> 00:03:08.090
Henry still wasn't sure that this counted as a mystery.

39
00:03:08.091 --> 00:03:12.341
But Nathan was their friend, and he seemed pretty worried.

40
00:03:12.342 --> 00:03:18.683
Besides, investigating a mystery was better than sitting around pouring lemonade all day.

41
00:03:18.684 --> 00:03:23.727
"We can look into it, I guess," Henry said.

42
00:03:23.728 --> 00:03:26.477
Cole picked up the five-dollar bill.

43
00:03:26.478 --> 00:03:30.187
"But you should take this back for now," he told Nathan.

44
00:03:30.188 --> 00:03:34.428
"What are you doing, Cole?" Maggie cried.

45
00:03:34.429 --> 00:03:39.145
"This may not be much of a mystery, but that doesn't mean we'll solve it for free!"

46
00:03:39.146 --> 00:03:42.963
"I know." Cole gave the bill back to Nathan.

47
00:03:42.964 --> 00:03:46.764
"But The Lemonade Detectives have a guarantee, remember?"

48
00:03:46.765 --> 00:03:53.523
He pointed to the line on their sign that read "All Mysteries Solved, Guaranteed."

49
00:03:53.524 --> 00:03:58.026
Maggie looked at it. "So what?" she said.

50
00:03:58.027 --> 00:04:04.161
"A guarantee means Nathan only pays us when he's satisfied with our work," Cole replied.

51
00:04:04.162 --> 00:04:08.435
"That's what my dad always tells his customers, and he's a businessman."

52
00:04:08.436 --> 00:04:13.342
"Well, we're not businessmen," Maggie said with a frown.

53
00:04:13.343 --> 00:04:18.844
"We're just kids. And I need that money for my riding lessons!"

54
00:04:18.845 --> 00:04:22.824
"We'll get the money as soon as we solve the case," Cole said.

55
00:04:22.825 --> 00:04:26.144
"Cole has a point, Maggie," Henry said.

56
00:04:26.145 --> 00:04:29.638
"It doesn't make sense for Nathan to pay us now.

57
00:04:29.639 --> 00:04:33.980
If we can't solve the case, we'll just have to give the money back."

58
00:04:33.981 --> 00:04:40.707
Maggie still looked unhappy. But she nodded. "Fine," she said.

59
00:04:40.708 --> 00:04:45.158
"I guess it doesn't matter as long as we solve this case fast."

60
00:04:45.159 --> 00:04:48.930
Nathan tucked the five-dollar bill back into his pocket.

61
00:04:48.931 --> 00:04:53.367
"So does this mean you'll try to solve my mystery?" he asked.

62
00:04:53.368 --> 00:05:00.119
"Yes," Henry said. "The Lemonade Detectives are on the case!"

63
00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:03.651
"Let's go to your house and talk to Nora," Cole said.

64
00:05:03.652 --> 00:05:07.510
There were no customers waiting for lemonade just then.

65
00:05:07.511 --> 00:05:12.518
Maggie took out a small sign that said "Back in a While" and set it on the table.

66
00:05:12.519 --> 00:05:21.879
Then they all walked over to Nathan and Nora's house.

67
00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:26.395
"Do you know where Nora is right now?" Maggie asked Nathan.

68
00:05:26.396 --> 00:05:29.860
"She's probably in the playroom," Nathan said.

69
00:05:29.861 --> 00:05:34.116
"It's at the back of the house so we can go in the back door."

70
00:05:34.117 --> 00:05:37.183
He led the way around the side of the house.

71
00:05:37.184 --> 00:05:41.235
They turned the corner just in time to see a window slide open.

72
00:05:41.236 --> 00:05:50.274
A second later Nora climbed out and tiptoed across the backyard!
